"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[55566],{55566:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n\\n## Convert AVI to MP3 with ffmpeg\\n\\nThere are times when you need to extract only the audio from a video file.  \\nWhen converting audio from AVI files to MP3, using <mark>ffmpeg</mark> is the simplest and fastest method.\\n\\nIf `ffmpeg` is not installed on your system, install it first using your package manager.\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Install ffmpeg on Ubuntu or Debian\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ sudo apt install ffmpeg\\n```\\n\\nOn macOS, install it with Homebrew (`brew install ffmpeg`).\\n```adcard\\n```\\n### Basic Audio Extraction (VBR)\\nThis is the default command to convert to high-quality MP3 using variable bitrate (VBR).\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Extract audio with VBR quality\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ ffmpeg -i input.avi -vn -c:a libmp3lame -q:a 2 output.mp3\\n```\\n\\nThe key options mean the following:\\n\\n- `-vn`: Disables video recording and extracts only the audio.\\n- `-c:a libmp3lame`: Encodes the audio in MP3 format (`libmp3lame`).\\n- `-q:a 2`: Sets the VBR quality level. Lower values yield higher quality, and setting it to `2` provides excellent quality around 190 kbps.\\n\\n### Fixed Bitrate (CBR) Extraction\\nIf you prefer a constant bitrate (CBR) instead of a variable bitrate, specify the `-b:a` option.\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Extract audio with fixed bitrate (192kbps)\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ ffmpeg -i input.avi -vn -c:a libmp3lame -b:a 192k output.mp3\\n```\\n```adcard\\n```\\n### Stream Copy Without Re-encoding\\nIf the audio codec included in the original AVI file is already MP3, copying only the stream with the <mark>copy</mark> option without re-encoding is much faster and involves zero quality loss.\\nHowever, if the audio uses a different codec such as AC3 or PCM, this method will fail or produce an unplayable file. First check the audio codec using `ffprobe`.\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Check the audio codec of the AVI file\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ ffprobe -v error -select_streams a:0 -show_entries stream=codec_name -of csv=p=0 input.avi\\nmp3\\n```\\n\\nUse the command below only when the output is `mp3`.\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Extract audio stream directly without re-encoding\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ ffmpeg -i input.avi -vn -c:a copy output.mp3\\n```\\n\\n### Batch Processing Multiple AVI Files\\nWhen converting all AVI files in a specific directory to MP3 at once, you can use a simple shell loop.\\nSince `*.avi` is case-sensitive, uppercase extensions like `.AVI` need to be run separately with `*.AVI`. If an MP3 with the same name already exists, ffmpeg will prompt whether to overwrite it; to overwrite without asking, add `-y`, or to skip, add `-n` before `-i`.\\n\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Batch convert all AVI files in the directory\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ for f in *.avi; do ffmpeg -i \\"$f\\" -vn -c:a libmp3lame -q:a 2 \\"${f%.avi}.mp3\\"; done\\n```"}')}}]);